{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-24T17:59:40.911555+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T17:59:41.435444+00:00", "id": 23623589, "conceptrecid": "23623588", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623588", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "metadata": {"title": "Empirical OEV & Liquidation Dynamics: 98.10% Value Recapture in Chainlink SVR Auctions and Structural MEV Power-Law Distribution on Ethereum L1", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<h2>Empirical OEV &amp; Liquidation Dynamics: 98.10% Value Recapture in Chainlink SVR Auctions and Structural MEV Power-Law Distribution on Ethereum L1</h2>\n<p><strong>Official Open Science Replication Package &amp; Empirical Benchmark</strong><br><em>Companion Research to the Werr Framework (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22939253\" rel=\"noopener\">Zenodo: 10.5281/zenodo.22939253</a> &bull; <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.25498\" rel=\"noopener\">arXiv:2609.25498</a>)</em><br><strong>Document ID:</strong> <code>WERRACLE-RES-2026-001-REV2</code> &bull; <strong>Date:</strong> October 24, 2026<br><strong>Lead Authors:</strong> Volkan Da\u011fl\u0131, Zerrin Da\u011fl\u0131, Da\u011fhan Da\u011fl\u0131<br><strong>Infrastructure &amp; Contributor Attribution:</strong> Bekirhan Da\u011fl\u0131 (ITouch Systems Research Desk, Adana &Ccedil;ukurova Teknokent, T&uuml;rkiye)<br><strong>Live Surveillance Observatory:</strong> <a href=\"https://radar.werracle.com\" rel=\"noopener\">radar.werracle.com</a> | <a href=\"https://werracle.io/radar.html\" rel=\"noopener\">werracle.io/radar.html</a> | <a href=\"https://api.werracle.com/v1/radar/overview\" rel=\"noopener\">JSON Telemetry API</a></p>\n\n\n<h3>Executive Summary &amp; Breakthrough Findings</h3>\n<p>Order Flow Auctions (OFA) and Proposer-Builder Separation (PBS) have fundamentally altered the landscape of decentralized finance (DeFi) liquidations. This open-science research package provides the complete, machine-audited dataset and companion monograph analyzing <strong>1,157 on-chain liquidations</strong> across <strong>Ethereum L1, Base L2, and Arbitrum</strong> during the severe market volatility regime of <strong>October 12&ndash;19, 2026</strong>.</p>\n<p>By deploying high-throughput WebSocket telemetry monitoring 83 Morpho Blue markets (over 280,000 flashblocks and 5.6M+ transactions decoded) coupled with atomic multi-call receipt decoders, this work presents the first independent empirical proof of <strong>Oracle Extractable Value (OEV) recapture</strong> under live market stress:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1. 98.10% Protocol Value Recapture:</strong> Across 105 verified Chainlink Smart Value Recapture (SVR) liquidations on Base Morpho Blue and Aave v3 totaling <strong>$190,506.31 in gross liquidated collateral</strong>, competitive solver bidding redirected <strong>$186,889.85 USD (98.10%)</strong> directly back to protocol reserves and depositors as competitive bids.</li>\n<li><strong>2. Bertrand Margin Compression &amp; Winner's Curse:</strong> Unconstrained price competition among permissionless solvers compressed gross margins to <strong>1.86% ($3,545.73 USD pre-swap)</strong>, with median margin settling at <strong>-1.55%</strong>. In <strong>61.9% of transactions (65/105)</strong>, solvers concluded at zero or negative net margin prior to off-chain DEX slippage. We document severe overbidding events (e.g. Tx <code>0x76a4c8...</code>) where solvers bid up to <strong>102.79%</strong> of collateral value, absorbing out-of-pocket losses of -$522.48 to win transaction inclusion.</li>\n<li><strong>3. Decentralization &amp; Absence of Monopolistic Capture:</strong> Active participation from <strong>20 distinct solver contract architectures and 27 signing EOAs</strong> confirms that order flow auctions maintain genuine Bertrand decentralization without cartelization. While solver <code>0x8b61...</code> won 48.6% of transaction counts by dominating micro-liquidations, its volume share was capped at <strong>31.64%</strong>, with independent solvers (<code>0x3ae5...</code>, <code>0xbd0d...</code>, <code>0xd128...</code>) driving competitive pressure on large liquidations.</li>\n<li><strong>4. Multi-Call Bundling Complexity (Methodological Advance):</strong> <strong>64.76% (68/105) of SVR transactions were atomic multi-calls</strong> executing up to <strong>32 liquidation sub-calls</strong> in a single transaction (Tx <code>0xc0a519...</code>, $20,969.08 gross). We demonstrate that naive single-event indexers miscalculate liquidation volume and solver PnL by failing to parse recursive sub-call execution trees.</li>\n<li><strong>5. Ethereum L1 Power-Law Distribution:</strong> Analysis of 1,049 Ethereum L1 liquidations reveals that <strong>80.84% (848 txs)</strong> of MEV-Boost block builder priority payments are micro-dust (&lt; $1.00 USD, median $0.08 USD), while the top 22 whale liquidations capture <strong>96.05% ($344,155.62 USD)</strong> of all builder revenue via private PBS bundles.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3>Package Contents &amp; Artifact Inventory</h3>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>File Name</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Empirical_OEV_and_Liquidation_Dynamics_Research_Monograph.pdf</strong></td>\n<td>PDF Preprint</td>\n<td>Camera-ready 3-page academic research preprint monograph with tables and charts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>EMPIRICAL_OEV_AND_LIQUIDATION_RESEARCH_2026.md</strong></td>\n<td>Markdown</td>\n<td>Full Markdown version of the empirical research monograph.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>data/werracle_oev_empirical_dataset_2026.json</strong></td>\n<td>JSON Dataset</td>\n<td>Audited dataset of 1,157 records (105 Base SVR, 3 Arbitrum SVR, 1,049 L1 events).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>scripts/verify_dataset_metrics.py</strong></td>\n<td>Python Script</td>\n<td>Automated test suite certifying all 15 core empirical invariants (100% pass).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>scripts/audit_multicall_bundle.py</strong></td>\n<td>Python Script</td>\n<td>Demonstration script inspecting atomic 32-call bundles and overbid dynamics.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>data/checksums.sha256</strong></td>\n<td>SHA-256 Hashes</td>\n<td>Cryptographic checksums for data integrity verification.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n\n<h3>Reproduction &amp; Verification Instructions</h3>\n<p>Any researcher or peer reviewer can independently certify the mathematical and statistical findings with Python 3:</p>\n<pre># 1. Clone repository or unzip package\nunzip zenodo_bundle_oev_liquidation_empirical_research.zip\ncd zenodo_bundle_oev_liquidation_empirical_research\n\n# 2. Run automated verification suite\npython scripts/verify_dataset_metrics.py\n\n# 3. Inspect multi-call atomic bundles and case studies\npython scripts/audit_multicall_bundle.py\n</pre>\n\n\n<h3>Institutional Attribution &amp; Computing Infrastructure</h3>\n<p>High-throughput bare-metal execution nodes (<code>pcworm-root</code>), archival RPC telemetry streams, and 24/7 continuous monitoring daemons were provided and sponsored by <strong>Bekirhan Da\u011fl\u0131</strong> (Managing Partner &amp; Co-Founder) and <strong>ITouch Systems Research &amp; Development Desk</strong> (Adana &Ccedil;ukurova Teknokent, T&uuml;rkiye).</p>\n<p><strong>Open Access &amp; Licensing:</strong> This work is licensed under the <strong>Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0)</strong>. Accompanying software tools are released under the MIT License.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Da\u011fl\u0131, Volkan", "affiliation": "Anadolu University", "orcid": "0009-0000-1587-8703"}, {"name": "Da\u011fl\u0131, Zerrin", "affiliation": "Mersin \u00dcniversitesi", "orcid": "0000-0001-9490-6425"}, {"name": "Da\u011fl\u0131, Da\u011fhan", "affiliation": "Toros Science High School, MEV", "orcid": "0009-0003-2492-8313"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Da\u011fl\u0131, Bekirhan", "affiliation": "ITouch Systems", "type": "Other"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/pCwOrM/werracle", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://radar.werracle.com", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "other", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://werracle.io/radar.html", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "other", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://api.werracle.com/v1/radar/overview", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "other", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22939253", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23623588"}}]}}, "title": "Empirical OEV & Liquidation Dynamics: 98.10% Value Recapture in Chainlink SVR Auctions and Structural MEV Power-Law Distribution on Ethereum L1", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623589", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623589?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23623589", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623588", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623588", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623588", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23623588", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23623589/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23623589/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.or