0-24T17:59:41.435444+00:00", "recid": "23623589", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "3717196f-aa44-4e2d-96a9-16dd0d6edc30", "key": "EMPIRICAL_OEV_AND_LIQUIDATION_RESEARCH_2026.md", "size": 14960, "checksum": "md5:aa41336ede6c3fe9729f90fefb93448d", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589/files/EMPIRICAL_OEV_AND_LIQUIDATION_RESEARCH_2026.md/content"}}, {"id": "cd86bf1e-43c1-4645-85a2-8bfa8dbc5c90", "key": "Empirical_OEV_and_Liquidation_Dynamics_Research_Monograph.pdf", "size": 113150, "checksum": "md5:c758c3197720e2d7136adf0896fad194", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589/files/Empirical_OEV_and_Liquidation_Dynamics_Research_Monograph.pdf/content"}}, {"id": "fb08c591-68cb-4f1d-9288-6a611afcc282", "key": "zenodo_bundle_oev_liquidation_empirical_research.zip", "size": 183964, "checksum": "md5:74c5fa7df485f2488ec6fa81d6d7c60e", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623589/files/zenodo_bundle_oev_liquidation_empirical_research.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1882756"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T17:48:25.271245+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T17:48:25.605096+00:00", "id": 23593165, "conceptrecid": "23593164", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23593164", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package: Standing on the Shoulders of Decaying Giants", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "publication_date": "2026-10-23", "description": "<p>Replication package of the paper \"Standing on the Shoulders of Decaying Giants\" (ICSE 2027, NIER track). The paper introduces tool decay: comparisons against a research tool lose validity because a replication package freezes the tool at release while the world moves on. We study it in merge conflict resolution.</p>\n<p>Contents:<br>- Citation analysis: 87 comparisons in 39 papers citing 41 merge-tool papers, and 237 maintainer updates to 35 tools. Includes the coding records, LLM pre-labeling runs, researcher adjudication and scripts (frozen).<br>- Exp 1 (field decay): 7 merge tools run as released on 1,700 Java merges from 410 GitHub projects (2010-2026). Includes the scenarios, the raw runs, the tool builds with their JDKs, and the scoring and statistics.<br>- Exp 2 (artifact decay): ChatMerge with its original LLM (gpt-3.5-turbo, retired), without it, and with the official successor model. Includes the recorded LLM answers.</p>\n<p>Every number and figure in the paper can be rebuilt offline from the raw runs (analysis/rebuild_all.sh, about 12 minutes); no merge tool is run and no LLM is called. Start with repo/README.md and repo/docs/replication.md. These cover the inputs, the commands, each paper number with its script, what cannot be rerun, and the third-party licenses. The data archives unpack into the repository snapshot (repo.tar.zst).</p>\n<p>Our code is under MIT and our data under CC BY 4.0. Third-party material keeps its own licenses (docs/third_party.md). Anonymized for double-anonymous review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Mouse, Anony", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["tool decay", "software ageing", "replication crisis", "empirical software engineering", "merge tools"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "empirical-software-engineering"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23593164"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package: Standing on the Shoulders of Decaying Giants", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23593165", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23593165?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23593165", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593164", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23593164", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23593164", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23593164", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23593165/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23593165/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23593165/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T17:48:25.605096+00:00", "recid": "23593165", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "37c95696-9293-4de9-8cb0-45f399fb75a3", "key": "replication_package.tar", "size": 1100195840, "checksum": "md5:b36867e04f0295333885e495cbfd63c6", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23593165/files/replication_package.tar/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1056997"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T15:04:33.270929+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T15:05:11.784661+00:00", "id": 23620725, "conceptrecid": "23591887", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23591887", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "metadata": {"title": "Replication Package of the Paper: \"Self-Admitted Technical Debt in AI-Intensive Cyber-Physical Systems: An Empirical Study\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<h2>Contents</h2>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Folder</th>\n<th>Contents</th>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/discovery/</code></td>\n<td>Repository metadata and discovery scores for 500 projects.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/analysis/</code></td>\n<td>The 1,500-record human&ndash;LLM dataset, 17,180 additional LLM classifications, classification inputs and counts for 117 repositories.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/extraction_used/</code></td>\n<td>Per-repository exports of the analyzed candidates.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/manual_classify/</code></td>\n<td>Master classification sheet and human&ndash;LLM comparison sheets.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/survey/</code></td>\n<td>Category-level and demographic survey aggregates.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>protocol/</code></td>\n<td>Taxonomy categories, LLM instructions, output schema and workbook prompts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scripts/archive/</code></td>\n<td>Repository discovery, historical SATD extraction and LLM classification scripts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>provenance/mining_logs/</code></td>\n<td>Compressed SATD extraction logs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>results/computed/</code></td>\n<td>RQ1 and RQ2 counts, repository distributions, false-positive counts and RQ3 aggregates.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>figures/</code></td>\n<td>AI-CPS taxonomy and practitioner criticality figures.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>survey/</code></td>\n<td>Practitioner questionnaire.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Setup</h2>\n<p>Install Python and Git. Open a terminal in the folder containing <code>requirements.txt</code>, then install the Python dependencies:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">python -m pip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre>\n</div>\n<h2>Repository discovery</h2>\n<p>Run the discovery script to generate a repository metadata CSV:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">python scripts/archive/discover_repositories_original.py --output repos_for_satd.csv --max-repos 500 --include-readme</code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>The command exports up to 500 repositories and includes README inspection. Other available settings are listed with:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">python scripts/archive/discover_repositories_original.py --help</code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>For authenticated GitHub requests, set the <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> environment variable before running the script.</p>\n<h2>Historical SATD extraction</h2>\n<p>Run the miner on the supplied repository list:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">python scripts/archive/mine_satd_original.py --input data/discovery/repos_for_satd.csv --output-dir satd_results --repo-cache tmp_repos --log-dir satd_logs --since-year 2022</code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>The script traverses available commits from the specified year, retrieves marker-bearing deleted source lines and their available pre-change context, and writes per-repository CSV files and logs. <code>tmp_repos</code> is the script's temporary clone directory.</p>\n<h2>LLM classification</h2>\n<p>In <code>scripts/archive/llm_classification.py</code>, replace the input, output and sample-count placeholders. For example, to classify the additional input:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">INPUT_FILE = r\"data/analysis/additional_input_17180.csv\"\nOUTPUT_FILE = r\"new_additional_llm_results.csv\"\nMAX_SAMPLES = 17180</code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>To use the initial subset instead, set <code>INPUT_FILE</code> to <code>data/analysis/manual_input_1500.csv</code> and <code>MAX_SAMPLES</code> to <code>1500</code>. The sample count must be an integer.</p>\n<p>Set the <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> environment variable, then run:</p>\n<div>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">python scripts/archive/llm_classification.py</code></pre>\n</div>\n<p>The script reads <code>ID</code>, <code>SATD_Keyword</code>, <code>SATD_Comment</code>, <code>Context_Type</code> and <code>Context_Code</code>, and saves broad classifications, AI-CPS categories and proposed category names. Checkpoints are saved beside the output. To resume an interrupted run, use the same input, settings and output path.</p>\n<h2>Results</h2>\n<p>The supplied summaries are in <code>results/computed/</code>. RQ1 percentages exclude false positives; RQ2 percentages use the AI-CPS-specific total within each analysis. Figures are supplied as PDFs in <code>figures/</code>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23591887"}}]}}, "title": "Replication Package of the Paper: \"Self-Admitted Technical Debt in AI-Intensive Cyber-Physical Systems: An Empirical Study\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620725", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620725?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23620725", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23591887", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23591887", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23591887", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23591887", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23620725/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23620725/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620725/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T15:05:11.784661+00:00", "recid": "23620725", "revision": 6, "files": [{"id": "00ad19bc-1530-42ea-8695-f0bc7c78226d", "key": "aicps-satd.zip", "size": 26454766, "checksum": "md5:840285cf23536d0a22a91757419fccca", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620725/files/aicps-satd.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "121709"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 4, "unique_views": 4, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T14:31:46.250298+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T14:31:47.058534+00:00", "id": 23620042, "conceptrecid": "23620041", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23620041", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "metadata": {"title": "Pacote de replica\u00e7\u00e3o \u2013 Trajet\u00f3rias letais tentadas e consumadas: an\u00e1lise comparada do feminic\u00eddio no Distrito Federal (2015\u20132026)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Material suplementar e pacote de replica&ccedil;&atilde;o do artigo \"Trajet&oacute;rias letais tentadas e consumadas: an&aacute;lise comparada do feminic&iacute;dio no Distrito Federal (2015&ndash;2026)\", submetido &agrave; Revista SUSP.</p>\n<p>O estudo compara 348 feminic&iacute;dios tentados e 241 consumados registrados pela CTMHF/SSP-DF entre mar&ccedil;o de 2015 e 31 de mar&ccedil;o de 2026, com qui-quadrado de homogeneidade (V de Cram&eacute;r) e raz&otilde;es de chance brutas com IC95% por bootstrap emp&iacute;rico (1.000 reamostragens, semente 42) para vinte vari&aacute;veis.</p>\n<p>O pacote cont&eacute;m:</p>\n<p>- replicacao_estatistica.py: script &uacute;nico que reproduz todos os testes do artigo (20 &chi;&sup2;, 12 raz&otilde;es de chance, testes de robustez do tempo de rela&ccedil;&atilde;o e cen&aacute;rio de Bonferroni) e confere cada valor com o publicado;</p>\n<p>- saida_replicacao.txt: registro integral da execu&ccedil;&atilde;o, com as vers&otilde;es do interpretador e dos pacotes (Python 3.12.3, numpy 2.4.4, scipy 1.17.1);</p>\n<p>- csvs/: tabelas de conting&ecirc;ncia extra&iacute;das dos relat&oacute;rios institucionais da CTMHF/SSP-DF (snapshot de 31/03/2026), uma por tabela do artigo;</p>\n<p>- README.md: instru&ccedil;&otilde;es de reprodu&ccedil;&atilde;o e descri&ccedil;&atilde;o dos procedimentos.</p>\n<p>N&atilde;o h&aacute; microdados. Os arquivos trazem apenas frequ&ecirc;ncias agregadas publicadas nos relat&oacute;rios institucionais, al&eacute;m dos 30 intervalos (em dias) entre intima&ccedil;&atilde;o da medida protetiva e fato fatal (Tabela 7), sem datas nem identificadores.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ferreira, Marcelo Zago Gome", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Bernardes, Paulo Henrique Marques", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Rozal, Regilene Siqueira", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Perazzoni, Franco", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Feminic\u00eddio", "viol\u00eancia de g\u00eanero", "medidas protetivas", "continuum da viol\u00eancia", "Distrito Federal", "Femicide", "Replication Package"], "dates": [{"type": "available"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "por", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23620041"}}]}}, "title": "Pacote de replica\u00e7\u00e3o \u2013 Trajet\u00f3rias letais tentadas e consumadas: an\u00e1lise comparada do feminic\u00eddio no Distrito Federal (2015\u20132026)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620042", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620042?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23620042", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620041", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620041", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23620041", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23620041", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23620042/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23620042/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23620042/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T14:31:47.058534+00:00", "recid": "23620042", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "353bcd11-2d3d-47d1-ae9d-12b18c84a70c", "key": "pacote_replicacao_SUSP_2026.zip", "size": 12878, "checksum": "md5:cbc060d949fe8f0d86621d9bbfdbb837", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23620042/files/pacote_replicacao_SUSP_2026.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1710303"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T12:00:47.915757+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T12:00:48.528274+00:00", "id": 23562419, "conceptrecid": "23562418", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23562418", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package: Review Automation and Human Participation in 2.6 Million GitHub Pull Requests", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "publication_date": "2026-10-22", "description": "<p>Replication package for the paper \"Review Automation and Human Participation in 2.6 Million GitHub Pull Requests\".</p>\n<p>Contents:<br>- github_prs_v2.parquet: 2,629,159 pull requests from 1,380 GitHub repositories (January 2019 to October 2026), one row per pull request, with per-row observation times. Human account logins are pseudonymised; free text is excluded.<br>- github_prs_v1_march2026.parquet: the initial March 2026 collection, used to validate fixed-window outcome measures.<br>- pr_reviews_v2.parquet: individual formal reviews with submission times for the 713,749 pull requests refreshed in October 2026, pseudonymised like the main dataset; input to the review-timing validation.<br>- pr_text_v2.parquet: pull-request titles and bodies with e-mails, human @mentions and sign-off trailers redacted, for text and NLP research.<br>- replication-package.zip: collection and analysis code, repository population and sample lists, account-classification rules (version 2.3.0), AI-reviewer registry, collection manifests, the review-timing validation, all analysis results and figure inputs.</p>\n<p>README.md gives a quick start, a command-to-output map for every figure and table in the paper, collection details and privacy notes. Code: AGPL-3.0. Data and results: CC BY 4.0 for the authors' contributions; content written by GitHub users remains subject to its authors' rights and GitHub's terms.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous Authors (under double-blind review)", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["code review", "pull requests", "generative AI", "bots", "GitHub", "empirical software engineering"], "version": "1.0-review", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23562418"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package: Review Automation and Human Participation in 2.6 Million GitHub Pull Requests", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23562419", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23562419?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23562419", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562418", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23562418", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23562418", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23562418", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23562419/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23562419/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23562419/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T12:00:48.528274+00:00", "recid": "23562419", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "46b65053-2013-402b-9586-23e68b91a38f", "key": "DATA_DICTIONARY.md", "size": 5367, "checksum": "md5:e1036380461a590e7b346d3381f26125", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/DATA_DICTIONARY.md/content"}}, {"id": "1740074b-a466-44a5-8554-de96ca60e2f6", "key": "CHECKSUMS.sha256", "size": 775, "checksum": "md5:0add57be9cb5ce1d9b848d01dee3f80d", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/CHECKSUMS.sha256/content"}}, {"id": "73dab05c-ab8b-4574-b2b8-6394311d2c28", "key": "README.md", "size": 11237, "checksum": "md5:9520c5b200a71a099a1f39cd7d58f4b4", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/README.md/content"}}, {"id": "0e3174ef-263e-48f3-b307-534bbce4ddaf", "key": "LICENSE-CODE.txt", "size": 34523, "checksum": "md5:eb1e647870add0502f8f010b19de32af", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/LICENSE-CODE.txt/content"}}, {"id": "145b59c6-06ba-4c36-99ed-872355168477", "key": "LICENSE-DATA.md", "size": 1546, "checksum": "md5:288635f2edfe08446011036a2bebb11c", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/LICENSE-DATA.md/content"}}, {"id": "dc659787-f419-44ea-9a61-655a58860cbb", "key": "pr_text_v2.parquet", "size": 820083143, "checksum": "md5:16e63c196f20d509ed411e3c76951004", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/pr_text_v2.parquet/content"}}, {"id": "493944bd-db9c-4b6c-a213-bc5d542df3a3", "key": "pr_reviews_v2.parquet", "size": 16176587, "checksum": "md5:8f06c9eb7b31268453cb8c9e6cc67c75", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/pr_reviews_v2.parquet/content"}}, {"id": "89b3318c-f204-46b6-a34d-c7b0a7cbf415", "key": "github_prs_v1_march2026.parquet", "size": 99493812, "checksum": "md5:54c5c4a045cf749aaff8bc774c30c3d0", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/github_prs_v1_march2026.parquet/content"}}, {"id": "9011610b-9a4c-447f-a24e-63ee1d08c0ba", "key": "github_prs_v2.parquet", "size": 121190951, "checksum": "md5:f4346550642ac405654eb03f46aab519", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/github_prs_v2.parquet/content"}}, {"id": "9b4fe174-b282-406e-b067-77e457662385", "key": "replication-package.zip", "size": 18442908, "checksum": "md5:a2e3f44e953efa6bf77697492a164efc", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23562419/files/replication-package.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1958287"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 1, "unique_downloads": 1, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 1, "version_unique_downloads": 1, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T11:42:38.381707+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T11:42:38.547640+00:00", "id": 23614176, "conceptrecid": "23614175", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614175", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "metadata": {"title": "Replication Package for \"Analysing Practitioners' Requests to Open-Source LLM Agent Frameworks and Harnesses\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<div class=\"split-container\">\n<div class=\"column preview-pane\">\n<div>\n<div class=\"content markdown-body\">\n<h1>Replication package</h1>\n<p><strong>Analysing Practitioners' Requests to Open-Source LLM Agent Frameworks and Harnesses</strong>(anonymous SANER submission; the manuscript is <code>docs/paper.pdf</code>).</p>\n<p>The study mines the requests that builders and users of LLM agents post to agent software: 334,646 issues and discussions of 152 popular open-source frameworks and harnesses on GitHub (July 2025 to October 2026), and posts on Hugging Face model pages and the Hugging Face Forum. It labels 6,620 of them, with a language model validated against AI references, by the part of the agent they concern (RQ1) and the help they ask for (RQ2).</p>\n<p>The package contains all code, the screening codes, the labelling guide, the prompts, the labels keyed by post identifiers, the validation scores and the aggregate results. <strong>It contains no post texts</strong>, apart from the short quotations that the paper prints, which its figure scripts contain. Every post is public and can be retrieved again from its identifier: <code>code/retrieve_texts.py</code> retrieves the texts of the labelled posts and of the GitHub threads (<code>docs/SOURCE_RETRIEVAL.md</code>).</p>\n<h2>Layout</h2>\n<p>Code and data are both split by the study's three phases: collection, validation (labelling) and analysis. Every folder marked with a README explains its contents.</p>\n<pre><code>replication_package/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 code/                    README: every script, in the order of the pipeline\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 collection/          github/, model_pages/, forum/, agent_terms/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 validation/          AI annotators, labeller, majority vote, failure fields\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 analysis/            analyses for RQ1 and RQ2 and their checks; paper/ writes the tables and figures\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 labels_table.py      writes data/labels.csv\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 retrieve_texts.py    retrieves the posts' texts into workspace/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 verify.py            checks of the package, and reruns\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 data/                    README: labels.csv, conventions, and every code in the data\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 labels.csv           one readable row per labelled post: identifier, address, labels in words\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 collection/          README: threads, discussions, topics, screening decisions, the sample\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 validation/          README: references/, labeller/ by stage, failure_fields/, results/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 analysis/            README: results/, and the paper's tables and figures as LaTeX\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 docs/                    README: the documents, and the study's earlier terms\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 paper.pdf\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 TABLE_MAP.md         every figure, table and number of the paper, mapped to its results file and code\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 METHOD.md            the method in brief\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 SOURCE_RETRIEVAL.md  retrieving the posts from their identifiers\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 codebooks/           screening codes, types of agent software, labelling guides, annotators' instructions\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 prompts/             the prompts of the production labeller and the failure fields\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 release/             inventory and checksums\n</code></pre>\n<p>The study's codebooks, scripts and results files use some earlier names than the paper (RQ3, kinds of help, readers for annotators); <code>docs/README.md</code> maps them to the paper's.</p>\n<h2>Choose a route</h2>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Goal</th>\n<th>Start here</th>\n<th>What it needs</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>See what each post was labelled</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/data/labels.csv\"><code>data/labels.csv</code></a>(<a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/data/README.md\"><code>data/README.md</code></a>)</td>\n<td>Nothing to run</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Check a number, table or figure of the paper</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/docs/TABLE_MAP.md\"><code>docs/TABLE_MAP.md</code></a>, then the frozen results in <code>data/</code></td>\n<td>Nothing to run</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Verify the package</td>\n<td><code>python3 code/verify.py</code></td>\n<td>Python 3.12 or newer, under a minute</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Recompute the estimates from the labels</td>\n<td><code>python3 code/verify.py --rerun</code></td>\n<td>Python 3.12 or newer, 8 to 15 minutes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Run a script by hand</td>\n<td><code>python3 code/verify.py --workspace</code>, then the script in <code>workspace/</code> (<a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/code/README.md\"><code>code/README.md</code></a>)</td>\n<td>Python 3.12 or newer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get the posts' texts back</td>\n<td><code>python3 code/retrieve_texts.py</code>(<a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/docs/SOURCE_RETRIEVAL.md\"><code>docs/SOURCE_RETRIEVAL.md</code></a>)</td>\n<td>Python 3.12 or newer, a GitHub token, about 30 minutes (an hour more with <code>--threads</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rebuild the corpus and the labels from scratch</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://markdownlivepreview.com/code/README.md\"><code>code/README.md</code></a>, \"Running the study again\"</td>\n<td>A GitHub token, the posts' texts retrieved again, and paid accounts with the model providers</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The code uses only Python's standard library, so nothing needs to be installed. The package was verified with CPython 3.12.11, 3.13.3 and 3.14.6. Two figure scripts use the f-string syntax of Python 3.12, so older versions cannot run them, and <code>code/verify.py</code> says so. <code>code/verify.py</code> never changes the package: its checks work in <code>reproduced/</code>, a scratch copy deleted afterwards, which needs about 350 MB of free disk (as does <code>workspace/</code>).</p>\n<h2>Verification</h2>\n<p><code>code/verify.py</code> runs these checks and prints PASS or FAIL for each:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Checksums:</strong> every file matches <code>docs/release/SHA256SUMS</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Prompts:</strong> every prompt matches its run's record: by its SHA-256 where the package ships it unchanged, and otherwise by containing the shipped labelling guide word for word.</li>\n<li><strong>Unit tests:</strong> the tests in <code>code/tests/</code> pass.</li>\n<li><strong>Tables and figures:</strong> all of <code>data/analysis/paper/</code> is rebuilt from the frozen results and compared byte for byte.</li>\n<li><strong>Production labels:</strong> the majority vote over the three production runs is recomputed and compared with the shipped labels.</li>\n<li><strong>Labels table:</strong> <code>data/labels.csv</code> is rebuilt from the shipped labels by <code>code/labels_table.py</code>and compared.</li>\n<li><strong>With <code>--rerun</code>, the analyses whose inputs are all text-free:</strong> the estimates of RQ1 and RQ2 with their bootstrap intervals, the failure fields, the robustness and validity checks, the explanatory models (E24 to E27), and the validation scores. Each is run with the arguments the study used, and its output is compared byte for byte with the frozen result. <code>explain.py</code> writes some keys in the iteration order of a set of strings, which changes from one Python process to the next, so a JSON output whose bytes differ passes if its parsed values are all equal, and the check says so.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>python3 code/verify.py</code> takes about 20 seconds. <code>--rerun</code> takes 8 to 15 minutes, depending on the machine's load, most of it in the bootstrap of <code>explain.py</code>. The numbers typed into the figure scripts and the paper's prose are traced in <code>docs/TABLE_MAP.md</code>, not checked automatically.</p>\n<p>The analyses that read the posts' texts need them: they match model versions, harness names or problem areas in the text (<code>model_releases.py</code> scan, <code>deepen_rq12.py</code>, <code>overlap.py</code>, <code>problem_areas.py</code>, <code>failures_exploratory.py</code>, <code>examples.py</code>). After <code>python3 code/retrieve_texts.py --replies --threads</code> they run in <code>workspace/</code> on today's versions of the posts; without the texts, they stop with an error or give meaningless results. The analyses whose inputs are other services' responses, which the package does not ship, cannot be rerun: the control projects' repositories and templates (<code>control_group.py</code>, <code>typed_baseline.py</code>, <code>agents_in_trackers.py</code>), the projects' discussion categories (<code>explain_rq3.py</code>), Stack Exchange (<code>stackoverflow.py</code>), the Wayback Machine (<code>agent_docs.py</code>) and the earlier Forum collection (<code>forums.py</code>). Their frozen results are in <code>data/analysis/results/</code>.</p>\n<h2>What is not in the package</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Post texts:</strong> titles, bodies, comments and replies, and the batches and prompts that embedded them; <code>code/retrieve_texts.py</code> retrieves the texts again.</li>\n<li><strong>Account names.</strong> Authors appear as salted pseudonyms (the same account has the same pseudonym everywhere), and the salt is not released. A post's author can still be read from the post itself, so the pseudonyms reveal nothing that the identifiers do not; they let the counts of practitioners (Fig. 1) and the authors' histories (E26) be rerun. Model owners' public namespaces on model pages are kept, since the analyses recognise the owners' replies by them.</li>\n<li><strong>Three inputs from outside the study's repository,</strong> needed only to rebuild the corpus: the earlier Hugging Face Forum collection (topics until September 2026), which belongs to another study (the package identifies only the Forum topics that this study used: 1,191 of the 4,022 in the window); a listing of all Hugging Face models (<code>HUB_LISTING</code>), from which the model pages' frame is drawn; and the identifiers of threads sampled by another study, against which <code>code/collection/github/sample.py</code> recorded the overlap of its draw.</li>\n<li><strong>The study's working documents:</strong> its protocols, which <code>docs/METHOD.md</code> summarises, the folders' notes, the codebook's superseded drafts, and the labeller's points to watch, which the shipped prompts contain.</li>\n<li><strong>Copies of development runs restricted to 524 of their 540 posts,</strong> whose labels are those of the full runs.</li>\n<li><strong>Raw API responses, budget ledgers, caches and logs.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Local paths, accounts and internal references are redacted wherever they appear, including the salts of the random draws, user-agent strings and the labeller's prompts. Because the salts change, a draw run again from the package differs from the shipped one, which is the draw the study made.</p>\n<h2>Licence</h2>\n<p>Code: MIT. Data, labels, prompts, guides and documents: CC BY 4.0 (<code>LICENSE</code>).</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous, Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23614175"}}]}}, "title": "Replication Package for \"Analysing Practitioners' Requests to Open-Source LLM Agent Frameworks and Harnesses\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614176", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614176?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614176", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614175", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614175", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614175", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614175", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614176/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614176/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614176/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T11:42:38.547640+00:00", "recid": "23614176", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "11c3fba1-d3bd-4a65-ad97-56d61ce4952d", "key": "replication_package.zip", "size": 36682934, "checksum": "md5:58006c23c35b4f51a93202f289adb8b6", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614176/files/replication_package.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "538803"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T10:11:25.171622+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T10:11:25.386376+00:00", "id": 23614953, "conceptrecid": "23614952", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614952", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for a performance experiment comparing Docker Desktop and Apple container", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Replication package for a performance experiment comparing <strong>Docker Desktop</strong> and <strong>Apple container</strong> (Apple's native container runtime for macOS) on Apple Silicon (M2 Pro).</p>\n<p>The methodology follows Raj Jain's framework (<em>The Art of Computer Systems Performance Analysis</em>, chs. 3 and 13): 30 iterations + 5 warmup iterations per benchmark, 95% confidence level, &plusmn;5% margin of error, and randomized execution order to eliminate systematic bias.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pereira, Alessandra", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de Pernambuco", "orcid": "0000-0002-5090-6762"}, {"name": "Zimmerle, Carlos", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de Pernambuco", "orcid": "0009-0008-7574-4190"}, {"name": "Gama, Kiev", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de Pernambuco", "orcid": "0000-0003-1508-6196"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23614952"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package for a performance experiment comparing Docker Desktop and Apple container", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614953", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614953?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614953", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614952", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614952", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614952", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614952", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614953/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614953/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614953/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T10:11:25.386376+00:00", "recid": "23614953", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "b19612ee-6a3b-4fa1-9956-bb8c71254fbc", "key": "docker-apple-container-performance.zip", "size": 17938690, "checksum": "md5:7592e0bfe67afeb7cad0c22277addb56", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614953/files/docker-apple-container-performance.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1962948"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T10:06:55.161987+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T10:27:23.452867+00:00", "id": 23615023, "conceptrecid": "23591659", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23591659", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package of (Promises and) Perils in Mining Hugging Face", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>This package contains the literature-screening records, paper-level coding, and model-level observations supporting the study <strong>&ldquo;(Promises and) Perils in Mining Hugging Face&rdquo;</strong>. The study examines how researchers sample Hugging Face (HF) models, which features they analyze, and which threats can arise from their sampling and measurement decisions.</p>\n<p>The package documents the evidence used to address three research questions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>RQ1:</strong> What sampling strategies are used in scientific research to analyze Hugging Face models?</li>\n<li><strong>RQ2:</strong> What features are analyzed in studies of Hugging Face models, and how are these features measured?</li>\n<li><strong>RQ3:</strong> What threats to validity and generalizability arise from sampling, measurement, and data-collection decisions when mining Hugging Face, and what practices can mitigate these threats?</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Contents</h2>\n<p>The package contains three workbooks and the forward-snowballing outputs:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text hljs plaintext\">.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.MD\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 ScopusRetrievedPaper.xlsx\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 RQ1_RQ2_Analysis.xlsx\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 RQ3_ModelsAnalysis.xlsx\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 forward-snowballing/\n</code></pre>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Contents</th>\n<th>Research questions</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ScopusRetrievedPaper.xlsx</code></td>\n<td>1,267 retrieved bibliographic records and three screening worksheets, with 44 records marked <code>Yes</code> in total.</td>\n<td>Corpus selection for RQ1&ndash;RQ2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RQ1_RQ2_Analysis.xlsx</code></td>\n<td>Descriptive inspection of 26 papers, 78 structured analytical records, and summary statistics.</td>\n<td>RQ1&ndash;RQ2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RQ3_ModelsAnalysis.xlsx</code></td>\n<td>Manual observations for 300 HF model repositories.</td>\n<td>RQ3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>forward-snowballing/</code></td>\n<td>Lists of citing papers and an analysis workbook supporting the Scopus-based literature search.</td>\n<td>Corpus selection for RQ1&ndash;RQ2</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Literature retrieval and screening</h2>\n<p><code>ScopusRetrievedPaper.xlsx</code></p>\n<p>The full-list export label identifies March 3, 2026. The bibliographic columns are <code>Rand_ID</code>, <code>Authors</code>, <code>Title</code>, <code>Year</code>, <code>Document Type</code>, <code>Source title</code>, <code>DOI</code>, <code>Link</code>, and <code>Abstract</code>. The screening worksheets additionally contain <code>Of_interest</code> and <code>Feature extracted</code>.</p>\n<p>The final analyzed corpus comprises the 26 papers represented in <code>RQ1_RQ2_Analysis.xlsx</code>.</p>\n<p>The <code>forward-snowballing/</code> folder contains lists of citing papers (<code>forward-*.csv</code>) and <code>Research Paper References.xlsx</code> used for forward snowballing to complement the Scopus search.</p>\n<h2>Paper analysis for RQ1 and RQ2</h2>\n<h3><code>Paper_Manual_Inspection</code></h3>\n<p>This worksheet contains 61 descriptive records covering 26 distinct paper links and 19 feature labels.</p>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Column</th>\n<th>Contents</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Feature_extracted</code></td>\n<td>Feature examined in the paper.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Methods_extraction_feature</code></td>\n<td>Description of how the feature was extracted or analyzed.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sources</code></td>\n<td>Artifacts or information sources used for the feature.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Metric</code></td>\n<td>Recorded measurement or characterization.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Link_Paper</code></td>\n<td>Link identifying the inspected publication.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling</code></td>\n<td>Descriptive indication of whether sampling was used.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Extraction_method_Paper</code></td>\n<td>Narrative description of collection and sampling procedures.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Claim</code></td>\n<td>Recorded findings or claims attributed to the inspected paper.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Threats stated by authors (related to HF data)</code></td>\n<td>Recorded threats attributed to the original authors.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Threats_introduced_by_extraction_method</code></td>\n<td>Assessment of possible threats associated with the extraction method.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Missing / additional threats (related to HF data)</code></td>\n<td>Additional methodological concerns recorded during inspection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Possible Threat introduced</code></td>\n<td>Further notes about potential threats.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3><code>Analytical_record</code></h3>\n<p>This worksheet contains 78 records with unique <code>Record_ID</code> values, covering 26 <code>Paper_ID</code> values and 19 <code>Feature_Code</code> values. There are <strong>59 distinct (<code>Paper_ID</code>, <code>Feature_Code</code>) pairs</strong>: the same pair can have multiple records describing different methodological choices.</p>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Column</th>\n<th>Contents or interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Paper_ID</code></td>\n<td>Paper identifier within this worksheet.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Record_ID</code></td>\n<td>Unique analytical-record identifier.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>DOI</code>, <code>Paper_URL</code></td>\n<td>Bibliographic identifiers for tracing the original paper.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling_Used</code></td>\n<td><code>1</code> for a sampled analysis; <code>0</code> for an analysis coded as using no sampling.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling_Strategy</code></td>\n<td>Recorded sampling strategy, including <code>NO_SAMPLING</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling_Unit_Code</code></td>\n<td>Entity sampled or analyzed, such as <code>MODEL</code>, <code>MODEL_CARD</code>, <code>DISCUSSION</code>, or <code>USER</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sample_Size_N</code></td>\n<td>Recorded sample size, where available.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling_Purpose_Code</code></td>\n<td>Purpose of the sampling or selection step.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Feature_Code</code></td>\n<td>Feature associated with the analytical record.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Population_Filter</code></td>\n<td>Population restriction, recorded separately from sampling.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Analysis_Scope</code></td>\n<td><code>FULL_HF</code>, <code>FILTERED_HF</code>, <code>SAMPLED_SUBSET</code>, or <code>FULL_AND_SAMPLED</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collection_Design_Code</code></td>\n<td>Collection-design label, including <code>NOT_REPORTED</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Analysis_Mode</code></td>\n<td><code>AUTOMATED</code>, <code>MANUAL</code>, or <code>HYBRID</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Analysis_Method_Code</code></td>\n<td>Coded extraction or analysis method.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Repository_Source</code>, <code>Metric</code></td>\n<td>Source and measurement associated with the record.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sampling_Basis_Detail</code>, <code>Analysis_Method_Detail</code></td>\n<td>Narrative details supporting the coded choices.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Paper_Evidence</code></td>\n<td>Recorded paper evidence supporting the extraction.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Source_Origin_Code</code></td>\n<td>Provenance label: <code>MANUAL_RQ1</code> or <code>ENRICHED_EXTRACTION</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3><code>DataStatistics_RQ1_RQ2</code></h3>\n<p>This worksheet stores summaries of sampling strategies, features, and analysis methods.</p>\n<h2>Model inspection for RQ3</h2>\n<p><code>RQ3_ModelsAnaysis.xlsx</code> contains:</p>\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Column</th>\n<th>Contents</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>model_id</code></td>\n<td>HF repository identifier, recorded on the first row of each model block.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>downloads</code></td>\n<td>Download count recorded for the model, on the first row of its block.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hf_url</code></td>\n<td>Repository URL, on the first row of its block.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>feature</code></td>\n<td>Feature inspected on the current row.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>value</code></td>\n<td>Recorded value or descriptive evidence, when populated.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>method1</code>, <code>method2</code></td>\n<td>Source annotations, such as metadata, model-card sections, or community sections.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>note</code></td>\n<td>Additional observations and possible discrepancies.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>owner</code></td>\n<td>Sparse free-text annotations concerning ownership or related observations.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The 24 positions in each model block cover all the features analyzed:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text hljs plaintext\">Bias; License; Dataset; Carbon Emission; Base Model; Spaces;\nModel naming; Number of parameters; Hardware and HF operating system;\nHyperparameter; Discussion; Model card Template (README); Like; Task;\nDownload; Lifespan; Model size (files); HF Library Usage; Code Example;\nQuantized; Adapters; Finetunes; Merges; Quantizations</code></pre>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous, Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23591659"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package of (Promises and) Perils in Mining Hugging Face", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23615023", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23615023?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23615023", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23591659", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23591659", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23591659", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23591659", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23615023/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23615023/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23615023/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T10:27:23.452867+00:00", "recid": "23615023", "revision": 6, "files": [{"id": "650eac94-6189-417b-a04e-208b3e08e839", "key": "replicationPackagePandPofHF.zip", "size": 2264895, "checksum": "md5:229145d473fd510ca708b6f5ec48def4", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23615023/files/replicationPackagePandPofHF.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1283979"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 1, "unique_downloads": 1, "views": 5, "unique_views": 5, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T09:45:27.131868+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T09:45:27.284557+00:00", "id": 23614579, "conceptrecid": "23614578", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614578", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"SpecVuln\" (anonymized for review)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Replication package for a paper submitted for double-blind review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Authors, Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23614578"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package for \"SpecVuln\" (anonymized for review)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614579", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614579?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614579", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614578", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614578", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614578", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614578", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614579/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614579/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614579/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T09:45:27.284557+00:00", "recid": "23614579", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "f957361e-faa7-4946-88fc-f4a4ad2b1cf3", "key": "dataset.csv.gz", "size": 1116368210, "checksum": "md5:370a1935afc91fab12d106c2fa63f6b4", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614579/files/dataset.csv.gz/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1428350"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 11, "unique_views": 4, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 4, "version_views": 11}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T09:27:18.680564+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T09:27:18.856483+00:00", "id": 23614280, "conceptrecid": "23614279", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614279", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "metadata": {"title": "Tiny Machine-Learning Operations within Cyber-Physical Systems: a Field Study [Replication Package]", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<h1>Trencher Predictive Modeling &mdash; TinyMLOps Replication Package</h1>\n<p>A reproducible TinyMLOps pipeline for predicting subsea cable trencher load peaks, accompanying the field study <em>\"Tiny Machine-Learning Operations within Cyber-Physical Systems: a Field Study\"</em>.</p>\n<h2>Setup</h2>\n<p>Requires Python 3.10 or newer:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">pip <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">install</span> -r requirements.txt\npip <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">install</span> -e .\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Configuration</h2>\n<p>All pipeline, feature-engineering, and modelling parameters are defined declaratively in <code>config.yaml</code>. Editing this file reconfigures domain-knowledge encodings, lag windows, and model hyperparameters without modifying Python code. Key sections:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>paths</strong>: input/output directories</li>\n<li><strong>importer</strong>: OSIsoft PI Web API (<code>pi_server_url</code>, <code>pi_dataserver_webid</code> placeholders) and PostgreSQL connection parameters</li>\n<li><strong>cleaner</strong>: KP column name and sensor-tag prefix stripping</li>\n<li><strong>constructor</strong>: soil-layer identifiers, burial-depth instruments, and file filters</li>\n<li><strong>peak_definer</strong>: rolling-window sizes and $\\sigma$ multipliers for load-peak labelling</li>\n<li><strong>model</strong>: declarative feature-aggregation schema (<code>X_agg</code>, <code>y_agg</code>) and regularised classifier hyperparameters</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Set your historian endpoint in <code>config.yaml</code> (<code>importer.pi_server_url</code> and <code>importer.pi_dataserver_webid</code>) and provide database credentials via <code>local_config.json</code> at the repository root (excluded from version control):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-json\">{\n&nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"osisoft_pi_username\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>,\n&nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"osisoft_pi_password\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>,\n&nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"D398\"</span>: {\n&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"user\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>,\n&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"password\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>,\n&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"host\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>,\n&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"port\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-number\">5432</span>,\n&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"database\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"...\"</span>\n&nbsp; }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Pipeline Steps</h2>\n<h3>1. Data Import</h3>\n<p>Requires access to an OSIsoft PI historian and/or PostgreSQL database containing the operational tables (<code>src/trencher/sql/kaskasi_cable_interval_importer.sql</code> shows the interval extraction query):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-title\">trencher</span>-<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">--source all</span>\n# or: python -m trencher.scripts.run_<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">--source pi</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>2. Data Cleaning</h3>\n<p>Extracts the longest monotonic Kilometre Point (KP) segment per cable pass and strips sensor-name prefixes:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">trencher-pipeline --<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">skip</span>-construct --<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">skip</span>-<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">aggregate</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>3. Physics-Informed Feature Construction</h3>\n<p>Aligns high-frequency sensor streams with geotechnical soil-layer profiles along KP, computes relative layer-proportion and boulder-risk features, and labels harmful Aft Cable Guide (ACG) load peaks:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">trencher-pipeline --<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">skip</span>-clean --<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">skip</span>-<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">aggregate</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>4. TinyML Pipeline &amp; Rolling Temporal Cross-Validation</h3>\n<p>Trains L1-regularised logistic regression (or Lasso) with interaction features under leak-free rolling temporal cross-validation and exports per-cable vs. cumulative coefficients:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">trencher</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">pipeline</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">skip</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">clean</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">skip</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">construct</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">cable</span><span class=\"hljs-literal\">-</span><span class=\"hljs-comment\">count</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\">100</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>5. Analysis &amp; Figure Generation</h3>\n<p>Generates descriptive time-series plots, per-cable correlation analyses, RQ2 boxplots, and out-of-sample South Fork validation figures:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">trencher-analysis <span class=\"hljs-comment\">--analysis all</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Supplementary Material</h2>\n<p>The <code>supplementary/</code> directory contains the non-proprietary campaign metadata tables and full per-cable evaluation figures referenced in the paper:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>supplementary/metadata/</code>\n<ul>\n<li><code>kaskasi_intervals.csv</code>: first-pass UTC start/end timestamps and durations for the 42 Kaskasi II inter-array cables (Sections III-D &amp; V).</li>\n<li><code>southfork_intervals_inc.csv</code>: first-pass UTC start/end timestamps and durations for the 11 South Fork Wind inter-array cables (Section VII-D).</li>\n<li><code>kaskasi_soil_layers_id.csv</code> and <code>southfork_soil_layers_id.csv</code>: geotechnical soil-layer identifier mappings (<code>L00</code>&ndash;<code>L09</code> / <code>L00</code>&ndash;<code>L08</code>) for both campaigns (Sections V &amp; VII-D).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><code>supplementary/figures/</code>\n<ul>\n<li><code>kaskasi_node_overview.png</code>, <code>kaskasi_cable_durations.png</code>, <code>oss_k29_soil_profile.png</code>: campaign layout, trenching durations, and representative soil-layer profile (Sections IV &amp; V).</li>\n<li><code>kaskasi_load_peaks/</code> and <code>southfork_load_peaks/</code>: full per-cable multi-window ACG load-peak classifications across Kaskasi II and South Fork Wind (Sections VII-A &amp; VII-D).</li>\n<li><code>soil_layer_coefficients/rq2_layer0.png</code>&ndash;<code>rq2_layer4.png</code>: per-cable vs. cumulative fitted coefficients and feature variance for soil-layer proportions <code>L00</code>&ndash;<code>L04</code> (Section VII-B).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Data Availability</h2>\n<p>Raw high-frequency sensor logs, Daily Progress Reports, and full geotechnical survey tables are proprietary to the industrial partner and cannot be publicly disclosed due to commercial confidentiality constraints. The complete <code>trencher</code> Python package, SQL extraction queries, declarative pipeline configuration (<code>config.yaml</code>), and supplementary campaign metadata and evaluation figures are released openly to ensure full inspectability and reproducibility of the pipeline architecture, knowledge-driven feature engineering, and rolling evaluation methodology. Researchers with access to analogous CPS telemetry can execute and adapt the pipeline via <code>config.yaml</code>.</p>\n<h2>Project Structure</h2>\n<pre><code>tinymlops-replication-package/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 config.yaml &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# Declarative pipeline &amp; feature configuration\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# MIT License\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/trencher/\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# Configuration loader\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 data/\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 importer.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# OSIsoft PI &amp; PostgreSQL data <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span>\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 cleaner.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Monotonic KP window extraction\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 constructor.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Soil-layer proportions &amp; peak labelling\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u2514\u2500\u2500 aggregator.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# Rolling-window signal aggregation\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 model/\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 pipeline.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# TinyMLOps training &amp; rolling CV pipeline\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u2514\u2500\u2500 peak_definer.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# Multi-window load-peak labelling\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 analysis/\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 descriptive.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Descriptive &amp; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">case</span>-study plots\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 correlation.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Per-cable correlation analysis\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 rq2.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # RQ2 peak vs. no-peak distributions\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2502 &nbsp; \u2514\u2500\u2500 southfork.py &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Out-<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">of</span>-sample South Fork plots\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 scripts/ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # CLI entry points (trencher-<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span>/pipeline/analysis)\n\u2502 &nbsp; \u2514\u2500\u2500 sql/ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # SQL interval extraction query\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 supplementary/\n&nbsp; &nbsp; \u251c\u2500\u2500 metadata/ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;# Campaign intervals &amp; soil-layer ID mappings\n&nbsp; &nbsp; \u2514\u2500\u2500 figures/ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; # Per-cable peak labels &amp; soil-layer coefficients\n</code></pre>\n<h2>License</h2>\n<p>Released under the <a href=\"LICENSE\">MIT License</a>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Scaramuzza, Filippo", "affiliation": "Tilburg University", "orcid": "0009-0007-9289-3182"}, {"name": "Tamburri, Damian Andrew", "affiliation": "Eindhoven University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0003-1230-8961"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23614279"}}]}}, "title": "Tiny Machine-Learning Operations within Cyber-Physical Systems: a Field Study [Replication Package]", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614280", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614280", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614280?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614280", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614280/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614279", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23614279", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23614279", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23614279", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614280/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23614280/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23614280