1897306, "checksum": "md5:a71bbfab1858c309fcf82f7bc7b556ed", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23606274/files/replication_package.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1185819"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 5, "unique_views": 3, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 3, "version_views": 5}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T00:14:37.617330+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T00:14:37.740129+00:00", "id": 23607107, "conceptrecid": "23578872", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607107", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23578872", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23607107", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Beyond Overt Toxicity: A Taxonomy and Human-LLM Analysis of Subtle Incivility on Stack Overflow\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607107", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>This package reproduces every number and figure in the paper. It contains the<br>annotation guidelines and the prompts given to the language models, the human<br>class and category labels for both 378-comment samples, the toxicity-classifier<br>and language-model outputs, and the scripts that recompute each reported result.</p>\n<p>Stack Overflow comment text is not included. The corpus is licensed to the<br>authors under an academic agreement that does not permit redistribution, so the<br>package keys on comment identifiers instead. Anyone holding the same corpus can<br>re-attach the text with a script we ship. Anyone who does not can work from the<br>forty paraphrased comments in data/artificial/, at least five per category, that<br>keep the behaviour each category names.</p>\n<p>code/analysis/verify_paper_numbers.py recomputes every reported figure from the<br>shipped files, needs no licensed data, and exits non-zero if any has drifted.</p>\n<p>See README.md for what each directory holds and how to run the checks.</p>", "acces